0576fed5fca2e9de51ca2e5e6649396a62994d1296de7","event_uuid":"a4ea3915-a1f9-4fbb-8b6e-919b640d4dde","position":{"commit_sha":"b69b919e22baf469b8caf4c79dce552299ef1766","position":"1786245480612856001-a4ea3915-a1f9-4fbb-8b6e-919b640d4dde"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7ef36b9084a3231e9b10a21778e6dceaa65ae3224484b8d2f00071742451a890","event_uuid":"dc4cea61-0aea-48c4-96fb-ee1e279b7b08","position":{"commit_sha":"9bc55be66c49c852f710513ac48b28a8436705dd","position":"1786245827158427001-dc4cea61-0aea-48c4-96fb-ee1e279b7b08"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"df1d5ccbc2adf075fc7b740a06f542be97cf65813c1c3e2188a198b60fd99c5d","event_uuid":"4c241aaa-0b2d-46ab-b7e2-11c0dadb747e","position":{"commit_sha":"8d589ed1b270dba9bf16c39de46b28bd3a36bcae","position":"1786247193394013001-4c241aaa-0b2d-46ab-b7e2-11c0dadb747e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PHASE-5 RESIDUAL-GAP DISPOSITION SWEEP (epic cf3c-1444-863e-49d7), before epic close.\n\nEnumerated gap sources across the run and their dispositions:\n1. cb91-1535-fe3a-47fc (generalize the self-contained 2-parent fold into a shared reconcile_one; discovered_from 0289) — FILED (open).\n2. 2207-2917-e21b-42bd (py3.11 opcert xdist worker-crash flake on test_matching_guard_is_accepted; discovered_from b014) — FILED (open). DEFINITIVELY proven base-wide/nondeterministic and independent of these changes: base sha 2d440ad668 itself crashes ~1/3 of runs identically and passes ~1/3; docs-only changes cannot affect opcert collection. Cleared by recheck.\n3. b014 review-plan advisories — NONE (final PASS had 0 advisory).\n4. Change 1552 (docs) LLM-Review advisories (PS1x1, PS2x2, non-blocking) — ACCEPTED: non-blocking advisories on a documentation-only change that merged LLM-Review+1 AND Verified+1; no behavioral surface.\n5. Change 1555 (docs) LLM-Review advisories — NONE.\n6. 0289 (change 1550, prior sessions) advisories (PS1x8, PS5x2, non-blocking) — ACCEPTED as non-blocking on merged code; the one substantive generalization gap is FILED as cb91.\n7. 4a surface-parity census — the S3 backend operation surface was delivered by the code stories (2b05/8970/0289) via the store/push/doctor seam and covered by their held-out oracles; b014 is a docs leaf introducing NO new operation surface -> N/A for b014.\n8. 4b excluded tests / 4e-bis escalation compromises — NONE (b014 is a non-code docs leaf; no implementer subagent, no held-out oracle).\n9. Landing-time deviation: ADR 0092->0093 renumber (collision with landed 0092-bridge ADR) — FIXED IN SCOPE (delivered as 0093 + delivery note in b014 description).\n10. Upstream git-remote-s3 README documents a stale lock-TTL env var (GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL); code reads GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS (verified against v0.3.2 tarball, tag=commit 9f3290e1, remote.py:95; the stale string appears in NO .py file) — FIXED IN SCOPE (flagged in docs + ADR with commit permalink and a verify-your-version hedge via change 1555).\n\nNo enumerated gap left without a disposition. Proceeding to close epic cf3c.","timestamp":1786245480612856001}],"created_at":1786149209026090001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3686e620-e2dc-4f34-ba9b-a1be61259f6b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6269-5b25-fe48-4c08"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nWe must deploy rebar where ticket data is sensitive and may **not** live in the GitHub\nrepo alongside source. rebar's ticket store is git history on an orphan `tickets` branch\nauto-pushed to `sync.remote` (`src/rebar/_config_schema.py` `SyncConfig.remote`,\n`src/rebar/_store/push.py:168` `push_tickets_branch`). We want that history in a\ncustomer-owned, SSE-KMS-encrypted S3 bucket instead of GitHub, keeping the identical\ngit/event data format and the auto-commit/auto-push flow.\n\nA live experiment (this session) proved the `awslabs/git-remote-s3` remote helper\n(Apache-2.0, actively maintained, git-bundle-per-ref + an `IfNoneMatch` per-ref lock)\nslots **below** rebar's shell-out git layer: pointing `sync.remote` at an `s3://bucket/prefix`\nremote makes init/create/claim/push/fetch work, and rebar's non-fast-forward recovery\n(`src/rebar/_store/push.py:51` `_is_non_fast_forward`) fires correctly because the helper's\nrejection surfaces as `! [remote rejected] ...`. Bundles were confirmed encrypted at rest\nwith a customer CMK.\n\nThe experiment also isolated the S3-**specific** risks this epic must own (rebar's\npre-existing best-effort-push and distributed-claim behaviors are **out of scope** — they\nreproduced identically against a GitHub-equivalent atomic-CAS remote):\n\n- **Multiple-bundles corruption**: concurrent/legacy pushes can leave two `<sha>.bundle`\n  files for one ref; `git ls-remote` then returns the ref at two SHAs and a fresh clone\n  **hard-fails** (`multiple updates for ref not allowed`) — the store becomes unclonable.\n  Upstream's `git-s3 doctor` repairs it but is **interactive-only** (crashes on EOF) and\n  **discards** a divergent head (data loss). Not usable for an autonomous agent fleet.\n- **Missing/old helper**: a client without the `IfNoneMatch` lock is what *creates* the\n  multi-bundle state; nothing currently stops such a client.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] rebar uses an `s3://bucket/prefix` value of `sync.remote` as a working ticket-store\n      remote — init/mount, create, claim, transition, and the push/fetch reconcile path all\n      succeed against it — with ticket data residing only in the SSE-KMS-encrypted bucket\n      (never in GitHub). Verified by an opt-in live integration test that drives those verbs\n      against a real ephemeral bucket and asserts a second clone reads the writes back.\n- [x] When `sync.remote` resolves to an `s3://` URL and the `git-remote-s3` helper is absent\n      or below the pinned minimum, store init and push **fail closed** with one actionable\n      message naming the exact `pip install`, instead of silently risking multi-bundle.\n      Verified by a CLI subprocess test asserting the message and a non-zero exit.\n- [x] The multiple-bundles state self-heals **non-interactively by merge**: after the heal,\n      `git ls-remote` returns exactly one bundle for the ref, a fresh clone succeeds, and\n      **every** commit/event from **all** divergent heads is reachable from the healed tip\n      (no head or event discarded). Verified by a real-git-repo test that forces two bundles\n      then asserts single-bundle + full-reachability.\n- [x] An operator can enable and configure the S3 backend from the documentation alone: the\n      optional `[s3]` dependency, the minimum helper version, SSE-KMS bucket + CMK/IAM setup,\n      and the `sync.remote=s3://…` configuration are documented. Verified by the docs child's\n      acceptance checks (files present and rendering the named sections).\n\n## Child decomposition (responsibilities; non-overlapping)\n\n- **Dependency plumbing** — declare the optional `[s3]` extra (`git-remote-s3>=0.3.2`) in\n  `pyproject.toml` and add an `_optional.py` probe + a `require_s3_helper()` availability/\n  version guard. Owns: dependency declaration and the pure availability check. Delivers AC-4\n  (dependency half) and the pin AC-2 depends on. No behavior wiring.\n- **Preflight enforcement** — wire that guard into `src/rebar/_store/push.py` and\n  `src/rebar/_commands/init.py` so `s3://` remotes fail closed when the helper is missing/old.\n  Owns: the fail-closed gate. Delivers AC-2.\n- **Auto-doctor (merge-heal)** — a new non-interactive self-heal that, on detecting the\n  multi-bundle signature during push, merges all divergent heads under a repo-level repair\n  lock and collapses them to one bundle. Owns: the healing mechanism. Delivers AC-3.\n- **Docs + ADR** — document the optional deps and S3 configuration, and record the\n  architecture decision (git-remote-s3 backend + merge-based auto-doctor). Owns:\n  documentation. Delivers AC-4 (docs half) and the AC-1 operator-facing configuration.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nrebar's pre-existing, backend-agnostic concurrency behaviors — best-effort push that can\ndrop an acknowledged write under heavy contention, and duplicate `claim` across separate\ncheckouts — are explicitly out of scope: the experiment reproduced both identically against\na GitHub-equivalent atomic-CAS remote, so they are not caused by S3 and belong to separate\ntickets. Lowering the helper lock TTL is also out of scope (a bounded 60s self-heal for a\nrare crash is acceptable; the helper already auto-steals a stale lock after TTL).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6269-5b25-fe48-4c08"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Container epic: all concrete file changes are carried by its child stories (dependency plumbing, preflight enforcement, auto-doctor, docs+ADR); the epic itself edits no files.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"bbb6538c-5c48-47a6-bb12-e58faf7b3bae","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"cf3c-1444-863e-49d7","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Support an encrypted S3 bucket as the rebar ticket-store remote (git-remote-s3) with S3-specific self-healing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f2f85902-80f6-4418-8d45-498da0005b30","92a47cbb-c9de-4cc5-8de7-d455d7edbbcc","482a1388-a60d-4ca1-9a41-07119d293918","8b41fc12-ad45-4832-89a9-74a0f1478628","3686e620-e2dc-4f34-ba9b-a1be61259f6b","bbb6538c-5c48-47a6-bb12-e58faf7b3bae","eeef582d-8406-4813-bd45-49d8d0cdbcc7","a4ea3915-a1f9-4fbb-8b6e-919b640d4dde","dc4cea61-0aea-48c4-96fb-ee1e279b7b08","4c241aaa-0b2d-46ab-b7e2-11c0dadb747e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786247193394013002,"uuid":"50fe8faa-cd86-4012-a650-b28c00439251"}